# Derived by hand from Semantics ch. 4 ("the order of a group's lines decides positions and nothing else"; a `rebuild` builds its first generation from the dynamic's value, `#0`), ch. 8 (a clause is chosen by its pattern) and ruling PL (a path is a list of lists, one per widget application; a building arm extends its list at the arm's position): loud gives the inner `if`'s 3, so `@Wide` at 1 builds "one 3" and "two 3" in its own list, the outer `if` at 2 builds the `rebuild` at its arm's 0 (`2.0.#0.0`, page 1) and the inner `if` at its arm's 1, whose label is `2.1.0` with page 1 doubled; soft gives 20 and builds nothing in its arm.
test loud

tick 0
  added:
    0: Ui.Button(label="go")
    1/0: Ui.Label(text="one 3")
    1/1: Ui.Label(text="two 3")
    2.0.#0.0: Ui.Label(text="page 1")
    2.1.0: Ui.Label(text="inner 2")

test soft

tick 0
  added:
    0: Ui.Button(label="go")
    1/0: Ui.Label(text="one 20")
    1/1: Ui.Label(text="two 20")
